{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Calibri;}}\fs22 Dear,\line \line We are ready to begin your transaction. Please Complete the Attached.\line \line Your project request has now been formally established within our system. To ensure proper documentation control and the efficient management of your transaction, all future communication and file uploads must be submitted directly within the designated project workspace once we have completed your project workspace. To help us do that, please reply to this message with the attached file completed.\line \line When accessing the Support Portal:\line \line -\line Log in and navigate to the Projects section.\line \line -\line Select \{project_name\} from your project list.\line \line -\line Use the Tickets tab for all communication, updates, and inquiries related to this project.\line \line -\line Use the Files / Uploads section for submitting all documents and materials relating specifically to this transaction.\line \line  Important  Only ONE Ticket Should Be Open Per Project\line \line To maintain clarity and ensure your transaction is processed efficiently:\line \line -\line Please keep only one active ticket open for each project.\line \line -\line All communication, updates, questions, and progress discussions for this project must continue within that single ticket thread.\line \line -\line Do not open multiple tickets for the same project, as this causes confusion for the relationship management team and may delay the handling of your work.\line \line We will continue to communicate back and forth on that single ticket until the project is fully completed.\line \line  Service Request Form & Multiple Transactions\line \line The Service Request Form included in your onboarding package allows us to determine and assign the correct project name(s), especially if you have multiple transactions.\line Each transaction will be organized under its own project, and all documents relating to that transaction must be uploaded exclusively within that projects file area.\line \line  Document Handling Requirements\line \line To maintain organizational integrity:\line \line -\line Please delete any files previously uploaded before this project was established, as they may cause confusion.\line \line -\line KYC documents for your banking profile must NOT be uploaded in the Support Portal.\line The banking system and the Premier Support Portal are separate, and KYC files must remain within the secure banking platform.\line \line Following these structured procedures ensures your transaction is handled accurately, securely, and expeditiously, with full transparency throughout the process.\line \line Should you require assistance navigating your project workspace, our support team will be pleased to assist you.\line \line Thank you for your cooperation and for choosing US Capital Private Bank.\line \line Thank you,\line US Capital Private Bank Client Relations}